   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Telling about an accident",
     "texto": [
      "To tell about an accident we use a verb with **me**, **te**, **se**… and the body part with an article, not with «mi»:\n\n- **Me he roto** el brazo.\n- **Me corté** el dedo cocinando.\n- **Me torcí** el tobillo.\n- **Me di** un golpe en la cabeza.\n\nThe pronoun already says whose arm it is, so we do not say «mi brazo».\n\nTo ask: **¿Qué te ha pasado?**, **¿Te duele?**\n\nTo treat it: a **tirita** (small wound), a **venda**, **hielo** or an **escayola** (broken bone)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Pronoun, article and tense",
     "texto": [
      "The body part takes **el / la** and the pronoun says whose it is:\n\n- **Me** he roto **el** brazo. (not «mi brazo»)\n- **Se** ha cortado **la** mano.\n\nTo tell the accident, three tenses combine:\n\n- **Imperfect** for the scene: **iba** en bici, **estaba** cocinando.\n- **Preterite** for what happens suddenly: **me caí**, **me corté**.\n- **Present perfect** if it is recent: **me he roto** el brazo."
     ],
